{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================================
  FILE LOCATION : templates/robots.txt.liquid    (Shopify theme > Templates)
  SERVED AT     : https://www.anandrasa.com/robots.txt
  ============================================================================

  DESIGN RULES FOR THIS FILE — read before editing.

  1. Shopify's `robots.default_groups` carries the platform-maintained crawl
     rules (blocking /cart, /checkout, /account, /admin, /search, faceted
     collection URLs, preview URLs and so on). Always emit them first and
     never replace them; Shopify updates them as the platform changes.

  2. The sitemap directive comes from `group.sitemap` — SINGULAR. An earlier
     revision of this file looped over `group.sitemaps` (plural), which is
     not a Liquid object, so it silently rendered nothing and /robots.txt
     shipped with no Sitemap: line at all. Do not reintroduce the plural.

  3. Naming a crawler in its own `User-agent:` group makes that crawler
     IGNORE the `*` group entirely. A bare `User-agent: X` + `Allow: /` pair
     therefore unblocks /cart, /checkout, /account and every faceted URL for
     that crawler. Any named group here must restate the protective
     disallows. That is what AR_AGENT_RULES below exists for.

  4. For the same reason, mainstream search crawlers (Googlebot,
     Googlebot-Image, Googlebot-News, Bingbot, DuckDuckBot, YandexBot,
     Applebot) are deliberately NOT given their own groups. They already
     match the `*` group, which allows the whole public site while keeping
     the transactional and duplicate surfaces blocked. Giving them a group
     would remove those protections and waste crawl budget. Leave them out.

     Google-Extended and Applebot-Extended ARE listed below because they are
     content-usage controls for AI training and answer surfaces, not
     crawlers — they have no crawl rules of their own to override.
  ============================================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- for group in robots.default_groups -%}
  {{- group.user_agent }}
  {%- for rule in group.rules -%}
    {{ rule }}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if group.sitemap != blank -%}
    {{ group.sitemap }}
  {%- endif -%}

{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Shared rule block for every explicitly named agent group below. Mirrors the
  protective disallows from the `*` group, then opens the rest of the site.
  Order matters: Allow: / is last so the specific disallows take precedence
  under longest-match resolution.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture ar_agent_rules -%}
Disallow: /admin
Disallow: /cart
Disallow: /carts
Disallow: /checkout
Disallow: /checkouts/
Disallow: /orders
Disallow: /account
Disallow: /search
Disallow: /a/downloads/-/*
Disallow: /recommendations/products
Disallow: /collections/*sort_by*
Disallow: /collections/*+*
Disallow: /collections/*%2B*
Disallow: /collections/*%2b*
Disallow: /blogs/*+*
Disallow: /blogs/*%2B*
Disallow: /blogs/*%2b*
Disallow: /*?*oseid=*
Disallow: /*preview_theme_id*
Disallow: /*preview_script_id*
Allow: /
{%- endcapture -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Generative AI, answer-engine and LLM-retrieval crawlers.

  OpenAI        GPTBot (training), OAI-SearchBot (ChatGPT Search index),
                ChatGPT-User (live in-chat fetches)
  Anthropic     ClaudeBot (index), Claude-User (live fetches),
                Claude-SearchBot, anthropic-ai (legacy)
  Perplexity    PerplexityBot (index), Perplexity-User (live fetches)
  Google        Google-Extended gates Gemini training and AI Overviews usage
  Apple         Applebot-Extended gates Apple Intelligence and Siri usage
  Microsoft     Copilot answers are served from the Bing index, which is
                already covered by the `*` group — no separate agent needed
  Others        Amazonbot (Alexa), DuckAssistBot (DuckDuckGo AI),
                Meta-ExternalAgent / Meta-ExternalFetcher (Meta AI),
                MistralAI-User, YouBot, cohere-ai, CCBot (Common Crawl,
                a training source for many downstream models)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ar_ai_agents = 'GPTBot,OAI-SearchBot,ChatGPT-User,ClaudeBot,Claude-User,Claude-SearchBot,anthropic-ai,PerplexityBot,Perplexity-User,Google-Extended,Applebot-Extended,Amazonbot,DuckAssistBot,Meta-ExternalAgent,Meta-ExternalFetcher,MistralAI-User,YouBot,cohere-ai,CCBot' | split: ',' -%}
{%- for ar_agent in ar_ai_agents %}

User-agent: {{ ar_agent }}
{{ ar_agent_rules }}
{%- endfor %}

{%- comment -%}
  Aggressive commercial SEO crawlers: permitted, but throttled so they do not
  consume the crawl capacity that matters for search and AI indexing.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign ar_throttled_agents = 'SemrushBot,MJ12bot,DotBot,BLEXBot' | split: ',' -%}
{%- for ar_agent in ar_throttled_agents %}

User-agent: {{ ar_agent }}
Crawl-delay: 10
{{ ar_agent_rules }}
{%- endfor %}

{%- comment -%}
  Policy and trust pages.

  Shopify's default `*` group blocks /policies/ wholesale. These five pages
  are self-canonical, return `index, follow`, and are linked from the site
  footer. They carry the shipping, returns, privacy and business-identity
  facts that E-E-A-T assessment and AI answer engines rely on, so they are
  re-opened individually. Longest-match wins, so these Allow lines override
  the broader `Disallow: /policies/` for these paths only; every other
  /policies/ URL stays blocked.

  Verified live 2026-08-31 — all five return HTTP 200. Re-verify before
  adding any new path here; a stale Allow pointing at a 404 is dead weight.
  A previous revision allowed /pages/faq, which does not exist on this store;
  the real FAQ handle is the one listed below.

  Note the closing tag below is `endcomment %}` without a trailing hyphen. The
  literal text that follows is not preceded by any Liquid tag that would emit
  a newline, so stripping here would weld `User-agent: *` onto the previous
  agent group's last rule.
{%- endcomment %}

User-agent: *
Allow: /policies/shipping-policy
Allow: /policies/refund-policy
Allow: /policies/privacy-policy
Allow: /policies/terms-of-service
Allow: /policies/contact-information
Allow: /pages/https-www-anandrasa-com-pages-frequently-asked-questions
